  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "A Muslim first name and a family name from the father. Many family names start with Ben (son of), like Ben Salah or Ben Amor, or name a place or tribe a family came from: Jlassi, Gharbi (from the west), Sfaxi (from Sfax), Hammami. First names mix classic ones (Mohamed, Fatma) with modern favourites like Skander, Eya, Yasmine and Wiem, written the French way. Young people often go by a short form: Hamma for Mohamed, Fatma for Fatima.",
